 chiral heterogeneous catalyst design&#10;principles to build a quantitative framework in which life-&#10;required functions are modeled as enantioselective&#10;recognition, catalysis, and transfer processes whose&#10;performance depends on chiral purity. Map homochirality to&#10;improved selec...&#10;justification: The candidate paper addresses how molecular and&#10;surface chirality produce enantioselective function, which&#10;directly supplies transferable quantitative concepts for&#10;evaluating why homochirality may enhance biological&#10;recognition, catalysis, replication fidelity, and&#10;coordinatio...&#10;abstract: A recent major focus of catalyst research has been&#10;on improving the selectivity or atom efficiency of catalytic&#10;processes. Perhaps the most subtle and difficult form of&#10;selectivity to control is enantioselectivity, a catalyst’s&#10;ability to preferentially yield one enantiomer of...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 6&#10;domain: materials_science&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Chirality in Supramolecular Assemblies: causes and&#10;consequences&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Chiral amplification through cooperative&#10;non-covalent interactions', 'Hierarchical transfer of&#10;stereochemical information from molecules to supramolecular&#10;assemblies', 'Majority-rules and sergeants-and-soldiers&#10;principles as quantitative models of symmetry breaking',&#10;'Coupling between chiral order and emergent functional&#10;properties such as recognition, catalysis, and transport',&#10;'Thermodynamic and kinetic selection mechanisms stabilizing&#10;homochiral assemblies']&#10;combination_plan: Use supramolecular chirality principles to&#10;build a quantitative multiscale model where enantiomeric bias&#10;propagates through cooperative interaction networks and&#10;modulates life-relevant functions such as molecular&#10;recognition, catalytic specificity, electron transfer, and&#10;repli...&#10;justification: The candidate paper addresses how c