transfer of&#10;stereochemical information from molecules to supramolecular&#10;assemblies', 'Majority-rules and sergeants-and-soldiers&#10;principles as quantitative models of symmetry breaking',&#10;'Coupling between chiral order and emergent functional&#10;properties such as recognition, catalysis, and transport',&#10;'Thermodynamic and kinetic selection mechanisms stabilizing&#10;homochiral assemblies']&#10;combination_plan: Use supramolecular chirality principles to&#10;build a quantitative multiscale model where enantiomeric bias&#10;propagates through cooperative interaction networks and&#10;modulates life-relevant functions such as molecular&#10;recognition, catalytic specificity, electron transfer, and&#10;repli...&#10;justification: The candidate paper addresses how chirality is&#10;organized, amplified, and functionally expressed in&#10;supramolecular systems, which provides a transferable&#10;mechanistic abstraction for linking molecular homochirality to&#10;higher-order biological functions without requiring direct&#10;do...&#10;abstract: [Back Cover] Supramolecular chemistry deals with the&#10;organisation of molecules into defined assemblies using non-&#10;covalent interactions, including weaker and reversible&#10;interactions such as hydrogen bonds, and metal-ligand&#10;interactions. The aspect of stereochemistry within such...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 3&#10;domain: computer_science&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: An optimal decoding algorithm for Molecular&#10;Communications systems with noise, memory, and pulse width&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Optimal decoding in noisy communication&#10;channels', 'Handling memory / intersymbol interference in&#10;sequential signals', 'Pulse-width or signal-duration effects&#10;on detection fidelity', 'Information-theoretic trade-offs&#10;between noise, memory, and decoding accuracy', 'Sequence-level&#10;decision rules rather than isolated symbol detection']&#10;combination_plan: Model homochiral biopolymers as information-&#10;transmission channels in which chirality acts as a coding&#10;constraint that improves decoding of molecular recognition,&#10;catalytic states, and replication outcomes under noise and&#10;memory. Use optimal decoding or information-capacity met...&#10;justification: Although the candidate concerns molecular&#10;communications rather than prebiotic chemistry, its&#10;abstraction of reliable signal decoding in noisy, memory-&#10;bearing channels maps naturally onto homochirality as a&#10;mechanism for improving molecular information fidelity,&#10;recognition sp...&#10;abstract:" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#ead1dc;strokeColor=#a64d79;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="11524" width="620" height="1194" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step8_selected_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step8_selected_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step_step9" value="Step 9 Idea Generation&#10;status: completed&#10;idea_count: 1&#10;round: 3" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="60" y="12818" width="220" height="96" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step_step8_step_step9" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step_step9"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step9_ideas_panel" value="Step 9 Idea Generation + Novelty Check&#10;count: 1&#10;&#10;1. Chiral kinetic proofreading: testing homochirality as an&#10;error-correcting code for electron-transfer assemblies&#10;novelty_level: medium&#10;motivation: The original question asks whether life requires&#10;chirality because handedness is merely a historical accident or&#10;because it solves a functional problem. Asymmetric autocatalysis&#10;can amplify tiny enantiomeric excesses [Author et al.,&#10;2020](https://openalex.org/W3210500841), nonequilibrium network&#10;models show how large systems can break chiral symmetry [Author&#10;et al., 2021](https://openalex.org/W3120596068), and pre...&#10;methods: 1. Defined chiral electron-transfer testbed: Create a&#10;minimal electron-transfer assembly whose geometry, redox&#10;spacing, and surface attachment are held constant while&#10;chirality is varied. Use self-assembling peptides or small&#10;protein domains bearing redox cofactors and terminal cysteines&#10;for electrode contact, as in studies of homochirality and&#10;electron transfer in protein assemblies [Author et al.,&#10;2023](https://openalex.org/W4384627421). Prepare all-L, all-D,&#10;alternating L/D, and racemic random versions, plus...&#10;novelty_justification: The proposal is not anticipated by the&#10;key references. The closest overlap is the combination of&#10;Examining the Effects of Homochirality for Electron Transfer in&#10;Protein Assemblies and Emergence of homochirality in large&#10;molecular systems, with secondary support from the prebiotic&#10;peptide-stability and Soai amplification papers. Together they&#10;supply the materials and context: chiral protein/peptide&#10;assemblies, elec...&#10;improvement_suggestions: ['Define a concrete molecular syndrome-&#10;detection rule that makes proofreading mechanistically distinct,&#10;for example a heterochiral junction produces a quantifiable&#10;cofactor misalignment, altered spin-selective dwell time, or&#10;exposed cleavage/ligation site that gates fuel hydrolysis only&#10;at defects.', 'Derive and test a minimal kinetic scheme showing&#10;that the repair cycle creates a discrimination factor beyond&#10;equilibrium binding, with measurable parameters for defect off-&#10;rate, correct-monomer reincorporation, ATP/fuel cost, and a&#10;threshold where proofreading outperforms passive&#10;stabilization.', 'Replace the generic editor with a minimal&#10;synthetic editor whose stereospecificity is built into the&#10;mechanism, such as a template-directed light- or ATP-driven&#10;exchange/ligation cycle that has opposite rate constants for&#10;correct- and wrong-handed monomers, thereby making the error-&#10;correcting code physically implementable rather than&#10;metaphorical.']" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="12818" width="680" height="924" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step9_ideas_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step9" target="step9_ideas_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="retrieval_1" value="Retrieval 1&#10;step: step1&#10;command: search-papers&#10;cache_hit: False&#10;paper_count: 18&#10;&#10;Parameters&#10;query_text: prebiotic symmetry breaking mechanisms&#10;generating enantiomeric excess&#10;keywords: [{'text': 'prebiotic symmetry', 'score': 10},&#10;{'text': 'symmetry breaking', 'score': 9}, {'text':&#10;'breaking mechanisms', 'score': 8}, {'text': 'mechanisms&#10;generating', 'score': 7}, {'text': 'generating&#10;enantiomeric', 'score': 6}]&#10;source_type: idea_text&#10;top_k: 18&#10;retrieval_mode: hybrid&#10;target_field: Chemistry&#10;&#10;Returned Papers&#10;1. In Situ Mass Spectrometric and Kinetic Investigations&#10;of Soai's Asymmetric Autocatalysis (2020) [score=0.7546]&#10;Abstract: Chemical reactions that lead to a spontaneous&#10;symmetry breaking or amplification of the enantiomeric&#10;excess are of fundamental interest in explaining the&#10;formation of a homochiral world. An outstanding example is&#10;Soai's asymmetric autocatalysis, in which small&#10;enantiomeric exc...&#10;&#10;2. Nonlinear Effects in Asymmetric Synthesis and&#10;Stereoselective Reactions: Ten Years of Investigation&#10;(1998) [score=0.6999]&#10;Abstract: Who would have thought before 1986 that an&#10;enantiomerically impure catalyst could give a product in&#10;an asymmetric synthesis with an enantiomeric excess higher&#10;than that of the catalyst? Until then it was assumed that&#10;the ee value of the product (ee&lt;sub&gt;prod&lt;/sub&gt; ) from an&#10;asy...&#10;&#10;3. SPONTANEOUS CHIRALITY OF THE ORGANIC ENVIRONMENT AS A&#10;SIGN OF EXTERNAL RADIATION EXPOSURE (2025) [score=0.6282]&#10;Abstract: This study investigates the phenomenon of&#10;spontaneous mirror symmetry breaking as a fundamental&#10;mechanism underlying the emergence of chiral purity in&#10;biological systems. It examines the transition from a&#10;racemic state, characteristic of inanimate matter, to the&#10;exclusive homo...&#10;&#10;4. In silico investigations towards homochirality in the&#10;context of the origin of life (2023) [score=0.615]&#10;Abstract: The future of the improvements of industrial and&#10;chemical processes is likely to be data-based. An&#10;elementary implementation for this are continuously&#10;developed tools to gain in-sights into complex reaction&#10;networks. This work provides insights into the design and&#10;ap-plication...&#10;&#10;5. Achiral 2‐pyridone and 4‐aminopyridine act as chiral&#10;inducers of asymmetric autocatalysis with amplification of&#10;enantiomeric excess via the formation of chiral crystals&#10;(2023) [score=0.5873]&#10;Abstract: Enantiomorphous crystals of achiral 2-pyridone&#10;and 4-aminopyridine served as sources of chirality, to&#10;induce the asymmetric autocatalysis of 5-pyrimidyl alkanol&#10;during the asymmetric addition of diisopropylzinc to the&#10;corresponding pyrimidine-5-carbaldehyde, that is, the&#10;Soai...&#10;&#10;6. From Ostwald Ripening to Single Chirality (2009)&#10;[score=0.5754]&#10;Abstract: A century ago Wilhelm Ostwald received the No