tric autocatalysis. Chiral symmetry breaking and&#10;the origins of homochirality of organic molecules (2019)&#10;[score=0.5465]&#10;Abstract: Biological homochirality, such as that of&#10;l-amino acids, has been a puzzle with regards to the&#10;chemical origin of life. Asymmetric autocatalysis is a&#10;reaction in which a chiral product acts as an asymmetric&#10;catalyst to produce more of itself in the same absolute&#10;configuration....&#10;&#10;13. Chirality amped up (2016) [score=0.5412]&#10;Abstract: N/A&#10;&#10;14. Can the analyte-triggered asymmetric autocatalytic&#10;Soai reaction serve as a universal analytical tool for&#10;measuring enantiopurity and assigning absolute&#10;configuration? (2016) [score=0.5352]&#10;Abstract: An investigation is reported on the use of the&#10;autocatalytic enantioselective Soai reaction, known to be&#10;influenced by the presence of a wide variety of chiral&#10;materials, as a generic tool for measuring the&#10;enantiopurity and absolute configuration of any substance.&#10;Good genera...&#10;&#10;15. Large Differences Between Stochastic and Deterministic&#10;Kinetics in a Simple Autocatalytic Reaction Network (2024)&#10;[score=0.5337]&#10;Abstract: In small systems, quantitative discrepancies&#10;between stochastic and deterministic descriptions of&#10;chemical kinetics can be significant, with their magnitude&#10;depending on the specific reaction network. Here, we study&#10;the Finke-Watzky model-an irreversible autocatalysis, A +&#10;B -...&#10;&#10;16. Exponential Amplification Using Photoredox&#10;Autocatalysis (2021) [score=0.5333]&#10;Abstract: Exponential molecular amplification such as the&#10;polymerase chain reaction is a powerful tool that allows&#10;ultrasensitive biodetection. Here we report a new&#10;exponential amplification strategy based on photoredox&#10;autocatalysis, where eosin Y, a photocatalyst, amplifies&#10;itself by...&#10;&#10;17. Chirality Selection Models in a Closed System (2004)&#10;[score=0.